Error [jet.RouteMethodTokenRefused]: HTTP route method `GET` is refused
  --> http_route_custom_method_standard.jet:9:16
    |
  9 |     mux.custom("GET", "/cache", handle).drop("route-check fixture")
    |                ^^^^^
 Why: `GET` is a standard method, which registers with its own verb `get`
 Fix: Register a standard method with its own verb (`mux.get`), and give `custom` any other token of letters, digits and !#$%&'*+-.^_`|~.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E2808
